      "narration_text": "Here's why. Divide one probability by another and the denominator cancels, leaving e to the score gap over T. Outcomes two and zero sit two points apart. At T point five, that ratio is fifty-four point six. At T two, two point seven two. Temperature stretches a gap; it never creates one.",
